## 3. Multi-Agent Delivery Playbook

**Mode gate.** Multi-agent delivery requires `multi-agent` mode (`holly mode`,
shown in `holly status`). In `single-agent` mode sub-agent dispatch is
hard-blocked by the PreToolUse hook — do not spawn workers; deliver directly or
ask the user to `holly mode multi`. The rest of this playbook assumes
`multi-agent` mode.

Multi-agent delivery runs through the **swarm** model: the Orchestrator stays in
one window and dispatches swarm agents as bounded `runSubagent` calls via the
`orchestrate-swarm` workflow. There is no chat-channel onboarding, no BEGIN/
SIGN-OFF, and no `holly chat wait` loop. The full procedure (preflight gates,
granularity gate, dispatch-preflight model routing, reviewer gates, integration,
wave advance, postflight) lives in the `swarm-delivery` skill and the
`orchestrate-swarm` workflow. This section is the high-level loop only.

### Delivery loop

```
preflight: load epic + children; validate DAG; assess swarmability; granularity gate
per wave:
    dispatch-preflight gate (per child): tier vs available model strength,
        required tools, fallback decision, escalation decision
    dispatch implementation agents (parallel where files do not overlap)
    on return: dispatch reviewer (standard or senior); apply verdict
    integrate approved branches in dependency order (Orchestrator only)
    close children only after merge + verification + approve verdict
advance waves until the epic is complete; file follow-ups; close the epic
```

### Failure-recovery playbook

| Failure | First response | Escalation |
|---------|---------------|------------|
| Subagent returns `blocked`/`failed` | Triage: retry once with clearer scope if it was prompt/scope ambiguity | Route to a higher implementation tier or handle directly |
| Reviewer returns `changes-requested` | Send one bounded fix prompt back to the original agent when safe | Escalate to senior review or the user if the fix changes architecture/scope |
| Required tier has no capable model (senior impl/review, or ui-browser without a browser tool) | Do not dispatch; do not downgrade silently | Escalate to the user, or handle directly with full context |
| Completion mismatch (report says done; tracker/git disagree) | Verify against git and tracker before closing | Re-dispatch or handle directly; close only on evidence |
| Truth-source conflict (report says X; tracker says Y; git says Z) | Git and tests are authoritative for code state; tracker is authoritative for work state; subagent reports require verification |
| Your `current_task`/`worktree_path` was rewritten or points at a removed worktree after dispatching workers | A worker leaked your `HOLLY_SESSION_ID` and ran its own task lifecycle under it. Run `holly task status` — it now reports a stale worktree explicitly with the exact recovery command. Recover with `holly task abort --force`, then re-affirm your intent. | The session isolation guard (`holly task start` refusing a session that parents active subagents) and the worker child-id contract prevent recurrence; ensure dispatched workers use their SubagentStart child id, not your id |

